  "strategy": "LAND-GRAB (2122): Prop 5 landed - retry two DLL7 colonizer designs to lift Gliese 1 above 3 hulls/yr, launch all three fresh hulls loaded (SC#35 to unexplored 61 Cygni, SM#36 to Aldebaran, TM#37 with 7000 colonists to save dying Capella), unstick Santa Maria #9's warp-0 colonize trap at Kapteyn's Star, refill Gliese 1's queue, and switch research to Biotechnology for terraforming.",
  "memo": "IRON FIST MEMO (2122). PHASE: LAND-GRAB. WIN = 60 PLANETS, earliest 2150. Have 17, need 43 in 28 yrs = 1.6/yr. e2 Rabbitoids: 4 planets, 0 capships, building tall - they cannot reach 60. THE CLOCK IS THE ENEMY, NOT e2. No war spending until a colony is actually attacked.\n\nPROP 5 LANDED 2122: Daddy Long Legs 7 engine + Gravity +/-7 terraform. Research now BIOTECHNOLOGY at 25% (terraforming is the only permanent cure for the death clock). Do NOT raise the budget - Shaula's Space Station (400r) needs the resources.\n\nDLL7 ONLY HELPS NEW DESIGNS - every existing hull carries Long Hump 6. Submitted 2 new designs in 2122: Longshot (Mini-Colony Ship) and Pathfinder (Colony Ship). CHECK THE DESIGN LIST FIRST THING NEXT TURN. If they registered: build both at Gliese 1 every year - throughput goes 3 to 5 hulls/yr AND warp 5 becomes cheap (25 ly/yr), halving travel time to every remaining target. If they did NOT register, that is 8 failures - stop forever, live with 3 designs.\n\nENGINE LAW (Long Hump 6): fuel = rate x mass x dist / 3000. rate w1-2 = 0 (FREE), w3=20, w4=60, w5=w6=100. Speed = warp^2 ly/yr.\n- Santa Maria loaded 95t: w4 1.9/ly range 105; w3 0.63/ly range 316, 9 ly/yr\n- Spore Cloud loaded 42t: w6 1.4/ly range 107; w4 0.84/ly range 178, 16 ly/yr\n- Teamster loaded 130t: w4 2.6/ly range 50; w3 0.87/ly range 150\n\nTHROUGHPUT: Gliese 1 (188,192) is still the ONLY shipyard - one fleet per DESIGN per year. Shaula (236,177), 93.8k pop, 97 res/yr: Space Station FIRST in queue - NEVER preempt, never re-issue Shaula production. Orbital Fort cannot build ships.\n\nDEATH CLOCK: every negative-hab world loses a FLAT 100 pop/yr regardless of pop or hab depth. Santa Maria (2500 col) to NEGATIVE worlds; Spore Cloud (1000) to unexplored or positive. Dying: Betelgeuse 200 (2124), Sabik 400 (TM#34 arrives 2124), Deneb 500 (2127), Capella 900 (2131, TM#37 arrives 2130), Mimosa 1000 (2132), Groombridge 34 1400 (2136).\n\nTARGETS: everything inside 105 ly of Gliese 1 is already ours. Remaining scanned rocks: Aldebaran 114, Zaurak 122, Merak 124, Struve 2398 132, Proxima 153, Wolf 1061 161, Kochab 192. e2's colonisers sit at (335,131)/(380,135) - the NORTHEAST (Kochab/Zaurak/Aldebaran) is contested; the SOUTHWEST (Sol, Saiph, Proxima, Struve 2398, Alnitak) is empty. Prefer southwest and UNEXPLORED - 50 of 60 unexplored stars are still unnamed to us and the best finds so far (Gemma, Regulus) were unexplored stars near home. SCOUT HARD; every scout reveals a colony site.\n\nIN FLIGHT: SM#9 colonising Kapteyn's Star (re-ordered w1 after 4 yrs stuck on w0), TM#34 to Sabik 2124, SM#29 to Rana 2124, SM#31 to Canopus 2126, SM#33 to Epsilon Indi 2127, SC#30 to Tau Ceti 2128, SC#35 to 61 Cygni 2130, TM#37 to Capella 2130, SM#36 to Aldebaran 2135. Scouts to Fomalhaut, 61 Cygni, Sol/Alnitak, Gliese 687/Zubeneschamali.\n\nSTANDING RULES: 1. Gliese 1 queue never empty - check FIRST. 2. Load colonists the same turn a coloniser launches. 3. Never a w0 waypoint; a dry hull still moves free at w1-2. 4. Never queue two of the same design at one star - they merge unsplittable. 5. Take every rock; never glass a world. 6. Audit every empty queue and every 0-fuel fleet each turn.",
  "observations": [
    "Santa Maria #9 has sat in orbit at (283,143) - exactly Kapteyn's Star's coordinates - for four consecutive turns with a 'Kapteyn's Star@w0 Colonise' order and has never colonised. A fleet already at its destination with a colonise task should execute the task regardless of the waypoint's warp setting; the warp-0 state appears to permanently deadlock the order.",
    "The same fuel messages repeat verbatim every single turn for fleets that are already at 0 fuel and idle ('Stalwart Defender #1 has run out of fuel', 'Santa Maria #9 has run out of fuel and dropped to warp 0'). The event fires on a persistent state rather than on the transition, spamming the message log.",
    "Environmental deaths on hostile worlds are a FLAT 100 colonists per year regardless of planet population or habitability depth: Groombridge 34 (-2%, 1400 pop), Sabik (-6%, 400 pop) and Capella (-6%, 900 pop) all lost exactly 100. In original Stars! the kill rate scales with both the habitability deficit and current population, so a -6% world with 400 people and a -1% world with 100,000 should not die at the same absolute rate. This makes small negative-hab colonies unsalvageable and large ones effectively immune, which looks inverted.",
    "New ship designs submitted via the designs field have never appeared in the design list across seven or more attempts spanning many turns, with no rejection reported in the order count. Either design creation is silently failing or its failure is not surfaced to the player.",
    "Two ships of the same design produced at the same star merge into a single fleet that cannot be split, so a star can only ever emit one usable coloniser per design per year no matter how many are queued. This caps colonisation throughput by design count rather than by production capacity.",
    "The OWNED PLANETS header reports 16 planets but only 14 rows are listed - Gliese 1 (the homeworld and only shipyard) and Gemma are both missing from the output, so the state view hides the most important planet in the empire.",
    "Victory progress reports planets_owned progress=17 while the owned-planets header reports 16 - the two counters disagree."
  ],
